[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Start "french-closed 7.Ne2"]
[Name "7...cxd4: the swap first"]

7... cxd4
8. cxd4 { The same reply: keep two pawns in the centre. The c3 square is free for a knight now. }
8... Qb6
( 8... Bb4? { Pins the knight, but there is nothing behind the pin to win, and the bishop is soon in the way. }
  9. O-O Be7 { The bishop has to go back, or it gets hit by a3. }
  10. Nf3 { White has developed two pieces while the bishop went there and back. The engine has White more than a pawn and a half ahead: the gain is positional. } )
9. Nf3 { The same move, and the same position as the main line by another order. } *
